{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/255823-the-masqu\u00e9-hall","id":255823,"title":"The Masqu\u00e9 Hall.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-12T21:52:12-07:00","id":255823,"title":"The Masqu\u00e9 Hall.","content":"Somewhere, among the twisting city streets, lies an old late 19th century theater. It's appearance decrepit and ill-kept, much akin to an old senile elder who's helper has left him. However, getting to this theater, while unadvisable, is a feat unto it's self that many a unfortunate soul has taken and fewer returned.<br /> <br /> You must walk during one of the equinoxes on a moonlit road heading north. The name of the road is unimportant, only that it's in the heart of the city and is covered by the light of the moon. Keep going forward. After the 12th road, you'll start to encounter road names that appear on no maps. Don't try to get your phone or it's GPS, reception is spotty at best and the GPS give wildly inaccurate positions and all your electronics will refuse to turn on by the time you arrive. You'll start to encounter new inhabitants. Creatures that wildly differ from size and shape and by all rights, shouldn't exist. Pay them no mind but know that most will attempt to hawk their wares. Ignore them if you can for what they are selling is often more than anything most are willing to provide.<br /> <br /> Don't bump into them or in anyway touch them, for if you harm them, they will seek reimbursement. A figure will appear, he will grab your hand, and cut off a finger before vanishing again at which point the offending creature will scamper off with your body part. If you suffer this, ignore the offense and carry on. For if you chase, more creatures will run your path and well... let's just leave at that.<br /> <br /> Continue on until you reach the end of the road. Looking upon it, you would be struck at it's age. It's skeletal frame jutting out of it's structure like broken bones jutting out of skin and yet it remains functional. The advertisements depends on what equinox you are currently on. For Spring, It will be advertising Romo and Juliet. For Fall, it will be Macbeth. A line for the ticker will have formed and simply fall in with the queue to wait your turn. It is advisable to avoid speaking to the other patrons but if you must, always remember to be polite for if you are rude, they will treat as a slight.<br /> <br /> You may notice that the ticker will payment in strange objects or relics. Fear not, for once he gets to you, he will simply hand you the ticket. If you ask why, the figure will say &quot;it's in the contract&quot; before getting the next person in line. You will then be escorted to your seat by mechanical figures. Always remain polite to them. If they ask to give you a refreshment, always ask for the price for if you don't, they'll assume you accept the implicit price that they are offering. Once in your seat, do your best not to bother the other patrons that may be around you for if you make a annoyance of yourself, you will be asked to join the staff on stage. You do not want to be on stage.<br /> <br /> As the curtains part, you will be introduced to the director of the show. mortal words simply fail to capture this being's aura and radiance and many who have witnessed it have reported one of there sense deadened for the next year and a day. However, it's is never the eyes nor the ears that are deadened for those still have a part to play.<br /> <br /> The play will then begin. It will begin jolly enough but if you are lucky..em, well unlucky that is, to be sitting near the front row or have exceptional eye sight, you begin to notice tiny strings attached to the limbs of the actors. Eyes that are a bit too wide to be acting. Flashes of metallic objects glancing off the stage lights. Pay close enough attention and you'll see the lips don't match the words, like a movie a half second out of sync.<br /> <br /> In the primary characters, it is most noticeable. Eyes wide with fear, limbs jerky, mouths move with such fury who's lines are heard a few seconds later and are clearly not the lines being mentioned. It's in the final acts that the fear really takes hold. The feeling of fore shadowing is implacable. You feel a chill run down your spine and somewhere deep inside your bones, you know that Death himself has just entered the room. You see the tension in the actor's limbs, the eyes growing wide with such creeping dread that you are reminded of a animal in a trap. Their mouths clearly not speaking the lines that you are hearing. You look around at the audience. Clearly they must be aware of the murder that is surely about to happen! How can they ignore this abominable execution! How can they-<br /> <br /> There is a clang of iron and steel. The final part has been played, the final lines said. You see the now prone bodies of the actors. Pale corpses, white as a fresh winter's snow with blood as red as late fall's leaves. The remaining actors bow and the curtain closes. Lights come back on and the mechanical figures come back to escort you out. They give no response to your questions and simply wish you well once you step out into the cold night air. The eccentric shops are now closed and all the creatures that you have seen, vanished. If you take a glance behind you, you'll find the theater lacking the supernatural vibrancy that had accompanied it earlier. Instead you see a dead corpse of a building, vacant and ancient.<br /> <br /> Walk the way you came, down the moonlit road. you'll eventually end up where you started the journey just as the sun is beginning to rise.<br /> <br /> If you wish, you can check the missing person's reports. You'll recognize some of the faces. It's not wise to go to the police about this, they've heard this story many a time and will most likely charge you for wasting theirs.<br /> <br /> So, if you're in for a good show and the seasons are just about right, travel down the moonlit road. The Masqu\u00e9 Hall waits for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 09-13-2014, 12:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}